# sweep: --bare
# An address typed on the reader and a key from the computer make the
# account. With no Miniflux server to answer, every sync and every feed
# added ends in a banner that names the real cause, and the address
# survives a restart.
wait-for Connect Miniflux
tap Type the address here
wait-for Server address
tap https://miniflux.example
wait-for Miniflux HTTPS server
type flux.invalid
tap Save
wait-for https://flux.invalid
clean
shot address-saved
tap Back
wait-for Unread
expect Starred
expect History
expect No unread articles
clean
shot shelf-empty
# No key yet: the sync says what is missing and which command adds it.
tap Sync
wait-for No Miniflux account is on this reader
clean
shot sync-no-key
companion secret set miniflux --from scripts/fixtures/rss-miniflux/token --sim
tap Sync
wait-idle 30000
wait 5000
wait-for Miniflux did not answer
clean
shot sync-unreachable
scenario offline
tap Sync
wait-idle 30000
wait 5000
wait-for This reader is not on Wi-Fi
clean
shot sync-offline
scenario normal
# With the last sync failed and nothing kept, no tab claims to be empty.
tap Starred
wait-for Nothing on this reader yet
expect-missing No starred articles
clean
shot starred-empty
tap History
wait-for Nothing on this reader yet
expect-missing Nothing read yet
clean
shot history-empty
tap Unread
wait-for Nothing on this reader yet
expect-missing No unread articles
restart
wait-for Unread
tap Settings
wait-for https://flux.invalid
tap Suggested feeds
wait-for NASA Science
tap NASA Science
wait-idle 30000
wait 5000
clean
shot add-feed-failed
# A feed that could not be added says so, not that a sync failed.
expect-missing Could not sync
